  "notes": "{投獄|とうごく} combines {投|とう} (throw) + {獄|ごく} (prison), literally \"to throw into prison.\" A formal term used in news, legal writing, and historical contexts.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {投獄|とうごく}する: to imprison\n- {投獄|とうごく}される: to be imprisoned (passive, very common)\n- {不当|ふとう}な{投獄|とうごく}: unjust imprisonment\n- {投獄|とうごく}される{恐|おそ}れ: risk of imprisonment\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {収監|しゅうかん}: confinement in prison (also formal)\n- {拘禁|こうきん}: detention, confinement\n- {禁固|きんこ}/{禁錮|きんこ}: imprisonment (as a legal sentence)\n- {懲役|ちょうえき}: imprisonment with hard labor\n\nREGISTER:\nThis is a written/formal word. In casual speech, {牢屋|ろうや}に{入|い}れられる or {刑務所|けいむしょ}に{入|はい}る are more natural.",
